# ── 3D construction scene (homepage "How we build") ─────────────────────────────
# Ops kill-switch for the WebGL scene. Set to "0" (or "false") to serve the static
# blueprint poster everywhere instead of mounting three.js — use if the scene ever
# needs to be disabled site-wide without a code change. Any other value / unset =
# scene enabled (default).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SCENE_V2=1

# ── Contact / enquiry form delivery (Web3Forms) ─────────────────────────────────
# Where leads from the Contact page + Home quick-enquiry form get emailed.
# Get a key at https://web3forms.com — enter the inbox that should receive leads
# (e.g. business@bdbuildcon.com) and they email you the access key.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and paste the real key there. .env.local is
# gitignored; never commit the real key. In production set the same variable in
# the host's environment settings (Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables).
#
# Left unset, submissions are logged to the server console instead of emailed,
# so local development still works without a key.
WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=
